<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Why the North Korean women's football team is so good</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3ae7a29440c934ac1afbf8ca5b98b8f41b793f5089b1778878bd16c297e583b</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-north-korean-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505--7a564644acc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-north-korean-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's young footballers enter the U-20 World Cup in Poland as defending champions — the 2024 title was their third. Why is the isolated state so good at the game?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football: Anyomi, London City and the German exodus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b33116ff4a858283b5702b6ec2e0aaa69117d59c3f4d7644c0efaa8b700f31c9</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131--1f6d62473b8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nicole Anyomi has joined Alexia Putellas and other star names in signing for the ambitious English club London City Lionesses. The Germany winger told DW England is a better place to develop her game than back home.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08296a90f4840d34dadbbbce75c3503a0913ae6dc39f76a6da46260a25ef8420</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578--3801f62b822d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austria are getting ready for their first Women's Ice Hockey World Championship. But preparations have been overshadowed by a dispute about conditions, pay and getting men's cast-off kit. A solution now looks in sight.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>New study shows German football remains male-dominated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5d2e59d5fe1099cdd00c6fe37421459febd4fda9cf7023737846b267ded4d2e</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569--b9ee319bf21e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-study-shows-german-football-remains-male-dominated/a-78532569?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The top leagues of German football remain a largely male environment. A new study reveals that only seven clubs have women in upper management levels.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA accuses UEFA of 'smear campaign' against Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fcec92a773de55afd3b8ee08638ce337bb48682ee02efc15b872afa19a9d938</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T03:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-accuses-uefa-of-smear-campaign-against-infantino/a-78896105--fcb4af3d736b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-accuses-uefa-of-smear-campaign-against-infantino/a-78896105?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The dispute between the two football associations reached a US court, in which UEFA is looking for permission to collect evidence for criminal proceedings in Switzerland.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa airline behind viral stadium flyby scraps repeat display</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d8badd8acfada3983466d0e9c01386054fb9b778f95930891ad3d2d9048128b</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-airline-behind-viral-stadium-flyby-scraps-repeat-display/a-78870028--ce70bf3d1027.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-airline-behind-viral-stadium-flyby-scraps-repeat-display/a-78870028?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two passenger jets passed close to Cape Town's DHL Stadium during a flyover last weekend. The carrier said it has shelved plans to repeat the display as South Africa's aviation authority investigates the event.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ailing Djokovic 'despised' every moment of US Open defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da24c006de9a24ebad783d27278ae4ad6811d5336a6e53b02593fa60511a44e0</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187--352c93994800.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Novak Djokovic has exited in the first round of a Grand Slam for the first time in over two decades. Could time — or an unknown health condition — be catching up with the Serbian tennis legend?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Andre Rankel named Germany's new men's ice hockey coach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcb491a55807e99c7479e1a54f50da013fe3a3ec4cf6b43fd1181faa2a31660d</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470--9672475007d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's men's ice hockey team has appointed a new head coach following a string of dissappointing tournaments. He's two decades younger than the man he's replacing but he has no previous experience as a head coach.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Venus' US Open invitation raises questions about wild cards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bfc44a1e379abef9bd5518e6f18ebf01d66aa998ac6989a0bac9afa90a652cb</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venus-us-open-invitation-raises-questions-about-wild-cards/a-78524056--49b415adc5c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venus-us-open-invitation-raises-questions-about-wild-cards/a-78524056?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although her current world ranking wouldn't allow it, Venus Williams is set to play singles in the US Open – thanks to a wild card. Who gets these coveted spots—and how?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bundesliga season 2026-27: All you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab4a61987b51fb28da8de696045be881ce9d1adf60c969c2e5af6fe35350f015</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T06:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-season-2026-27-all-you-need-to-know/a-78061925--f39290153444.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundesliga-season-2026-27-all-you-need-to-know/a-78061925?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From key dates to rising football stars and changes, DW has the latest on the new Bundesliga season.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Reports: UEFA backs off FIFA boycott threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24fbacb6989aafef435cc70b1df354da98708b280c24120d054f83f118a440f4</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T13:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/reports-uefa-backs-off-fifa-boycott-threat/a-78511519--372fe96c45a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/reports-uefa-backs-off-fifa-boycott-threat/a-78511519?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">UEFA is reportedly set to withdraw a threat to boycott FIFA tournaments over a plan to partially privatize football tournaments. The Under-20 Women's World Cup is to be hosted by Poland next month.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The new Bundesliga season is here, but has the glow gone?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76fb767ab323116e82279d7805b591e0c479c4c258c72b6511ef88a26bb63322</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032--f578ab52d735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Another Bundesliga season arrives, but are the golden years of Germany's top football league already over, and what can it do to change its course?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>UEFA, other football federations unite against Infantino</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:030ebf4fcf3181e2033b775e54e5c80cb33fa25c9c2fa6b6dabb67a2cd463625</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T11:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601--e313c442a148.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uefa-other-football-federations-unite-against-infantino/a-78301601?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A few weeks ago, Gianni Infantino looked set for another unopposed term as FIFA president. Now, with an election looming, the beleagured football executive is counting the numbers and could be hanging by a thread.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How Gianni Infantino rose to rule football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdecc3a2711e321ef8617572a4be568de6c56805850ff51101b6fa511fe75f08</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:59:44Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T12:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-gianni-infantino-rose-to-rule-football/a-78242568--63c1ed54d01d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-gianni-infantino-rose-to-rule-football/a-78242568?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Gianni Infantino is staying on as FIFA president despite growing pressure to step down. So who is football's most powerful man, why did UEFA and others turn against him, and how did he reassert his authority?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
